  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Unknown Song** (1 review): Vocal isolation suggests the unidentified track is actually the song Gypsy [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Ants and Bats**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Good to Me**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Lunch Meat**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Fried**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Unknown Song**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Ghost- Goodnight Owl (Cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Eddie Cousin**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **kglw2011-02-12** (recommended): source not stated; 7 songs; 30 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The performance was likely a late Christmas function for Victorian publication Forte Magazine [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **kglw2011-02-12**: taped by Unknown; transferred by doctordarkroom [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by KGLW.net: [King Gizzard & the Lizard Wizard setlist - 2011-02-12 Geelong Gaol Museum, Geelong, VIC, Australia](https://kglw.net/setlists/king-gizzard-the-lizard-wizard-february-12-2011-geelong-gaol-museum-geelong-vic-australia.html) [6]\n- Poster by KGLW.net: [Geelong Gaol, by King Gizzard & the Lizard Wizard / Releases / KGLW.net](https://kglw.net/discography/geelong-gaol) [7]",
